<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24688" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδέρκομαι</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έδρᾰκον,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>see</i> one thing
			<i>through</i> another, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἂν νῶϊ
				διαδράκοι</span>
			<i>would</i> not <i>see</i> us <i>through</i> [the cloud],
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.344
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>look about,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντῃ δὲ διέδρακεν ὀφθαλμοῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					25.233
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>see over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cypr.
					11.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
